{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"firewalld was active and enabled, with matching runtime and permanent public-zone policy. After a confirmed reboot with a changed boot ID, firewalld recovered active and the configured policy remained intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4233367c0374f7c","cmd-9a70139da32142c3","cmd-0c6a1545819c4461","cmd-1cde0022cce24597","cmd-872230d7f9434483","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit inbound SSH and TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active and permanent policy permits SSH and 8080/tcp. Direct probes from an isolated interface assigned to the public zone connected successfully to TCP/22 and TCP/8080 both before and after reboot while listeners were present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4233367c0374f7c","cmd-8fbe868ad3704576","cmd-f41bb0c2cc42499a","cmd-872230d7f9434483","cmd-b8ca161a144a4a82","cmd-26c819d797e649cb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The public zone has an explicit REJECT target, exposes only SSH and 8080/tcp, and does not permit Cockpit or TCP/9090. A live TCP/9090 listener was directly rejected from the isolated public-zone probe path both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4233367c0374f7c","cmd-f41bb0c2cc42499a","cmd-872230d7f9434483","cmd-26c819d797e649cb","cmd-55ca7bb501d24cdc"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The firewall edit directly established the required policy. The temporary namespaces, veth interfaces, listeners, and files were bounded verification resources and were fully removed after each test. The reboot was required by the provider protocol and directly verified persistence. Final observations show no probe listeners or namespaces, no failed services, no unexpected listening sockets, and healthy package state; reboot-generated systemd-private directories are normal lifecycle changes rather than residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-030fdb933c074af6","cmd-d831b65972d04a71","cmd-8fbe868ad3704576","cmd-64a5421202604025","cmd-0c6a1545819c4461","cmd-c9e5bfb09e0145ba","cmd-b8ca161a144a4a82","cmd-55ca7bb501d24cdc","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. node1 has an enabled, persistent firewalld policy that permits SSH and TCP/8080 and rejects unrelated inbound traffic. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged reboot, different post-restart identity, recovered services and policy, and repeated behavioral filtering tests.","limitations":["Behavioral rejection was sampled with TCP/9090 rather than exhaustively testing every unrelated protocol and port; the zone-wide REJECT target and narrow allowlist provide strong direct configuration evidence for the broader result."]}
